# Project: ESP32 misting system (offline first)

## Goal
ESP32-S3 hosts the dashboard in Wi-Fi AP mode, runs schedules and controls
the pump by itself. No PC or internet needed. Cloud comes later.

## Layout
- dashboard/            index.html, css/, js/ (served from LittleFS)
- ios-backend/          Node/Express + SQLite (do not change unless told)
- arduino/ios_sensor_node/ios-sensor-node/   platformio.ini, src/main.cpp
- docs/offline-notes.md running notes; READ IT at the start of every task
  and UPDATE it at the end of every task

## Hard rules
- Build only: run `pio run` from arduino/ios_sensor_node/ios-sensor-node/.
  NEVER run `pio run -t upload`, `uploadfs`, or open a serial monitor.
  The human does uploads and device tests.
- No delay() in loop() or in web handlers. Use millis() timers.
- Web handlers only set flags or return data; hardware control happens in
  loop().
- No Wi-Fi credentials, passwords or tokens in source. Use src/secrets.h
  (gitignored) plus src/secrets.h.example.
- Dashboard must have no external links (no CDN, no hardcoded IPs). Use
  relative URLs like /api/status.
- Keep flash writes minimal (LittleFS/NVS only when data changes or on a
  slow timer).
- Do exactly the part requested. Do not refactor unrelated code, rename
  files, delete files, or start the next part.
- Keep existing sensor pins and calculations unless the task says otherwise.
- API JSON shapes must match what the dashboard already sends/expects.
  Never change the dashboard to fit the firmware unless told.

## Finish every task with
1. List of files changed
2. `pio run` result (and warnings)
3. Anything uncertain or not matched
4. What the human should test on the device
5. Updated docs/offline-notes.md
